: it is behind 25% of your lost leads, 1.3\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the king's knight (61%), landing on e5, e4, d5.","Aim at their bishop: it is behind 20% of their lost leads, 1.3\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the light-squared bishop (62%). The reply wins it outright 23% of the time. Take it with a bishop.","Material changes hands for you on e5 and d4: build pressure there.","They win material on d5 and f7: keep those squares defended.","Look for the trapped piece: it appears 2.0\u00d7 as often as usual in this opening."],"similar":[],"family":"French Defense"}